import{_ as a,o as t,c as s,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CyZTVJbV.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"announcements/v1.29/x-thread-en.md","filePath":"announcements/v1.29/x-thread-en.md"}'),i={name:"announcements/v1.29/x-thread-en.md"};function r(n,e,c,d,p,l){return t(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<p>1/ kiwa v1.29 is out — release script filter systematic root cause SSOT milestone. After 4 milestones (v1.14 payment / v1.25 perf-harness / v1.27 quality-metrics / v1.28 realtime) rediscovered the exact same &quot;package missing from either build filter or publish filter half&quot; bug, v1.29 stacks <strong>4 layer automation</strong> (release-smoke test axis + PostToolUse hook + SSOT docs + new npm package) to close the release-gate final hole. Runtime fixture count 34 → 35 (<code>@kiwa-test/release-invariants</code> v0.1.0 new). 7-milestone snippet validation streak (v1.23-v1.29). 3 sub-Issue merges.</p><p>2/ The bug that recurred 4 times — <code>pnpm -F {name} build</code> (build filter) and <code>pnpm publish --filter {name}</code> (publish filter) are 2 separate halves inside <code>scripts.release</code>. A contributor adds a new package to one half. The release runs green — the build produces the artefact, the publish command exits 0 because the packages it was told about succeeded. The registry never receives the new package. v1.14 payment / v1.25 perf-harness / v1.27 quality-metrics / v1.28 realtime each hit it independently.</p><p>3/ v1.29-1 release-smoke test axis (Issue #986, PR #989) — <code>tests/release-smoke/tests/release-script-filter.test.ts</code> (167 lines) with dynamic package discovery + 40 per-package <code>it.each</code> assertions. Walks <code>packages/*/package.json</code>, filters by <code>@kiwa-test/*</code> scope + <code>private: false</code>, checks each publishable package appears in <strong>both</strong> halves. Fail-fast <strong>before</strong> the milestone finisher. Landed 6 previously-missing packages (agent / ai-llm / component / mcp / search / streaming) in the same PR.</p><p>4/ v1.29-2 PostToolUse hook + <code>/issue-plan</code> checklist SSOT (Issue #987) — <code>hooks/post-tool-use/release-script-filter-guard.sh</code> proactive prevention. When Write / Edit tools touch <code>packages/*/package.json</code>, the hook scans the root <code>package.json</code> release script for the package&#39;s filter presence and warns (does not hard-deny) if either half is missing. <code>/issue-plan</code> skill body embeds a checklist for new package additions so the invariant is called out in Issue body before implementation.</p><p>5/ v1.29-3 release-invariants v0.1 + docs + publish (Issue #988) — new npm package <code>@kiwa-test/release-invariants</code> with 3 pure invariant checkers + a 1-shot aggregator. <code>checkReleaseScriptFilter</code> (both halves per package), <code>checkProvenanceFlagAbsence</code> (v1.14 removed <code>--provenance</code> from <code>pnpm publish</code>, must not creep back), <code>checkGateScriptPackageCoverage</code> (<code>test:mutation</code> must cover every publishable package), and <code>buildReleaseInvariantsSummary</code> (1-shot summary with <code>ok: boolean</code>). 8 behavior test PASS.</p><p>6/ Why a new package (not just internal tests)? The 3 invariants are pure functions with no kiwa-specific dependencies. Any pnpm monorepo can call <code>buildReleaseInvariantsSummary({ releaseScript, mutationGateScript, publishable })</code> from a test runner or a plain node script. The SSOT ships as an npm package so downstream users can adopt the pattern without copying kiwa&#39;s internal code.</p><p>7/ 7-milestone snippet validation streak — <code>packages/release-invariants/tests/docs-tutorial-v1.29.test.ts</code> (8 test) re-runs every code snippet from <code>docs/tutorials/55-release-script-filter-ssot.md</code> against the real <code>@kiwa-test/release-invariants</code> v0.1 API. Continues the streak: v1.23 payment / v1.24 edge / v1.25 perf-harness / v1.26 orm / v1.27 quality-metrics / v1.28 realtime / v1.29 release-invariants. Any docs drift is structurally blocked.</p><p>8/ docs — tutorial 55 (<code>release-script-filter-ssot.md</code> 15-min walkthrough with mock adapter + file adapter + 4 RED/GREEN behavior tests) + concept doc (<code>release-invariants.md</code> = 3 invariants catalog + systematic root cause pattern + 4-time rediscovery ledger + 7-milestone snippet validation streak) + migration guide (<code>v1.28-to-v1.29.md</code> additive-only, breaking change 0). VitePress sidebar wired + <code>/docs-publish-kiwa</code> gh-pages published.</p><p>9/ 18-milestone streak — v1.11 → v1.12 → v1.13 → v1.14 → v1.15 → v1.16 → v1.17 → v1.18 → v1.19 → v1.20 → v1.21 → v1.22 → v1.23 → v1.24 → v1.25 → v1.26 → v1.27 → v1.28 → v1.29. Every milestone since v1.11 has landed sub-Issues in full. v1.29 is the lightest sprint yet (3 sub-Issue, 4-layer automation, 1 new npm package). Roadmap: <a href="https://github.com/cardene777/kiwa#roadmap" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://github.com/cardene777/kiwa#roadmap</a></p>',9)])])}const v=a(i,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,v as default};
